## Realism / weak recovery
Good: partners stripping `=` from urlsafe dest tokens is a real JWT/PLC footgun (`urlsafe_b64decode` on the raw string raises Incorrect padding); padding then `base64.b64decode` is the equally tempting std-alphabet wrong fix and the mixed-pad test names the contract (`cmFkYXI` plus PLC `cmFkYXItaGV4_w` both decode, not 13 leftover data characters). `fifo_queue = true` without a `.fifo` name is the usual CreateQueue reject; `name=.fifo` with `fifo_queue=false` still cannot satisfy a test that requires FIFO plus `content_based_deduplication`. Stale 502 fallback now compares dest want unpadded `_` tokens / live `.fifo` against a second file still on `cmFkYXI=` (r61 densification). Reviewer keep-b64decode is an explicit rejected keep-wrong-fix (r64 densification). hcl2json at the plan-change names fifo_queue vs suffix as two fields rather than a single jq blob. gate-cli freeze plus refuse-destroy is an honest apply block, not a silent skip. Weak: PLC trailer `\\xff` is baked into token.py rather than read from fixtures/radar.ndjson in the same turn; FIFO test still uses a list of asserts instead of a tflint-fixed fifo-only module. Next densification: a 502 whose local radar-tokens fixture is rewritten after the urlsafe pad patch and still lists `cmFkYXI=`, or a reviewer asking to keep `fifo_queue=false` "so operators can still grep standard queues from runbooks".

Novel coverage: 46%
